A class attribute is now inferred with the values assigned to it through the
class, as in ``cls.attr = value`` in a class method or ``Klass.attr = value``,
along with the value set in the class body. Only the latter used to be
inferred, so pylint reported ``unsubscriptable-object``,
``unsupported-membership-test`` and similar errors on lazily initialized class
attributes such as ``cache = None``.

Closes pylint-dev/pylint#9250
Closes pylint-dev/pylint#9809
Closes pylint-dev/pylint#10082
Refs pylint-dev/pylint#3045
